<title>UK: No proposal to suspend current ACPC export quotas.</title>
<headline>No proposal to suspend current ACPC export quotas.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delegates to the Association of Coffee Producing Countriess (ACPC) technical group meeting said that there was no proposal to suspend the current export quota programme for arabica coffees.</p>
<p>President of Costa Rica's Ecafe exporter group Ricardo Seevers said that &quot;There is no such proposal,&quot;</p>
<p>There were earlier reports that Colombia would raise the question of quota suspension at the meeting in view of the recent high prices.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
